<http://data.silknow.org/object/242680d0-ed8a-3f78-aa35-bf9611807bf0/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Panel. gray-green satin ground, with pattern brocaded in polychrome silks and silver yarn. Symmetrical design showing a flowery grove by a wall with a waterfall and certain bizarre elements such as giant bud or horn with flames at its crest, and curved bars at base of waterfall. Both selvedges, one partly broken away: six white cords, black wefts. Soiled and faded; silver tarnished; blacks mostly rotted out, leaving satin warps loose."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/242680d0-ed8a-3f78-aa35-bf9611807bf0> .

